<title>INDIA: India says to float 25 bln rupees state govt loans.</title>
<headline>India says to float 25 bln rupees state govt loans.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Finance Ministry said on Wednesday that the first tranche of state government loans for 1997/98 (April-March) will be floated on April 30 for 25 billion rupees.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that the loans will be of 10-year maturity and carry an annual coupon rate of 13.05 percent.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
